# Private functions
  -- Rotated text
  @fn rasteriseRotated(ctx, s, size)  @ 37-76
  @fn rotatedTex(ctx, s, size)  @ 80-87
      -- pcall doubles as the js_ReaScriptAPI presence check; a failure caches
      -- false so callers fall back for good.
  -- Label wrapping
  @fn camelSplit(word)  @ 102-113
      -- Split a word at CamelCase boundaries. Plugin and track names are ASCII in
      -- practice, so raw byte-class checks (no utf8) are sufficient.
  @fn atomise(text)  @ 117-129
      -- Tokenise into atoms with per-pair separators: seps[k] joins atoms[k..k+1] when
      -- they share a line — ' ' between words, '' between CamelCase pieces, so a rejoined line has no added space.
  @fn joinAtoms(atoms, seps, i, j)  @ 131-135
  @fn balancedLines(atoms, seps, maxW, maxLines, widthOf)  @ 140-171
      -- Balanced break: a line costs the square of its slack, and the cheapest split
      -- wins, which also settles the line count — see docs/arrangePage.md § Grid is hand-drawn.
      @contract  nil when atoms can't fit — one wider than the box, or more lines needed than maxLines  @ 139
  @fn gamma(x)  @ 394-399
  @fn oklchToRgb(light, chroma, hueTurns)  @ 401-413
  @fn hueRGB(idx, chroma, light)  @ 417-419
      -- Golden-ratio rotation throws adjacent indices to opposite sides of the
      -- wheel; light/chroma are held constant so the set stays perceptually even.

# Public API (painter.*)
  @api painter.measureRotated(ctx, s, size)  @ 90-94
      @contract  strip (w,h) in screen px for textUp at this size; nil when the LICE path is unavailable  @ 89
  @api painter.wrapLines(text, maxW, maxLines, widthOf)  @ 175-217
      @contract  text as <=maxLines lines each <=maxW by widthOf, surplus ellipsised onto the last line  @ 173
      @contract  widthOf measures in the font the caller draws in, or the lines overflow the fitted box  @ 174
  @api painter.new(ctx, chrome, transform, page)  @ 220-388
      @contract  sx/sy default 1 and must be non-zero (fromScreen divides); ox/oy default 0.  @ 219
  @api painter.hue(idx, chroma, light, alpha)  @ 423-426
      -- The idx-th perceptually-even hue. chroma/light/alpha tone it.
      @contract  returns an opaque colour token (not a bare int); pass to a draw method's colour arg.  @ 421
  @api painter.hueNative(idx)  @ 429-435
      @contract  REAPER native int (|0x1000000 set) for I_CUSTOMCOLOR; chroma/light match grid fill hue.  @ 428

